stateDiagram-v2
  accTitle: The three autonomy modes
  accDescr: The operator starts the master in one of three modes. Autonomous keeps taking queue rows until the queue is empty or every row waits on a decision. Finish and stop lands what is in flight and takes nothing new. One ticket lands one and reports. Any mode stops on an unexplained red check or a safety rule, and waits for the operator's go.
  direction LR
  state "Autonomous" as Auto
  state "Finish and stop" as Finish
  state "One ticket" as One
  state "Stopped, report sent" as Stopped
  state "Blocked, operator asked" as Blocked
  [*] --> Auto : keep going
  [*] --> One : one ticket
  Auto --> Finish : finish and stop
  Auto --> Stopped : queue empty or all rows blocked
  Finish --> Stopped : in-flight tickets landed
  One --> Stopped : ticket landed
  Auto --> Blocked : unexplained red or safety rule
  Blocked --> Auto : operator's go
  Stopped --> Auto : operator's go
